The function calls `fetch(...).then(...)` but never awaits it, so `return profile.name.toUpperCase()` runs immediately, while `profile` is still `undefined`. This throws `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'name')` on every call, since the assignment `profile = data` happens asynchronously, after the function has already returned.

